[{'id': 5501349, 'title': "Open website in the user's default browser without letting them launch anything else?", 'body': '<p>I would like to open a website in a user\'s default web browser, however since the url is user-defined I would also like to prevent them from doing anything other than opening a website.</p>\n\n<p>I have seen people use <code>Process.Start(url);</code> to open a site in the default browser, but since the url is user-defined I want to be sure they don\'t enter something like a script location and execute it. </p>\n\n<p>I also don\'t want to use <code>Process.Start("iexplore", url);</code> since I would rather open the link in the user\'s default browser.</p>\n\n<p>Is there a way I can open a website in the user\'s default browser, without letting them launch any other process or command?</p>\n\n<p><strong>EDIT</strong></p>\n\n<p>For example, I don\'t want users to be able to enter <code>C:\\Windows\\Notepad.exe</code> into the Customer\'s Website field and open 


